# Backend coverage

- Follow the backend coverage requirement in `AGENTS.md`.
- Keep both SonarQube Overall Coverage and Coverage on New Code strictly above 80%; target at least 81%.
- Add tests with behavioral assertions for success, invalid input, missing resources and conflicts. Include duplicate/concurrent execution and rollback where relevant.
- Run `test jacocoTestReport` using the backend Gradle wrapper. Inspect uncovered lines and branches before adding tests.
- Run `scripts/sonar.ps1` from the repository root when local SonarQube is available; verify the completed analysis and Quality Gate.
- Never lower thresholds, expand exclusions, remove tests or add tests without meaningful assertions to satisfy coverage.
- Preserve user data and use a separate database for integration tests.
- Report actual metrics and any verification blockers; do not claim coverage passed without measurement.
